data: {"item_id":"rs_515505","output_index":0,"sequence_number":466,"summary_index":0,"text":"We need to implement the task. The previous attempt had a patch command that was malformed. Need to create repository with proper files: server.js, maybe a simple HTML in public folder, and client JS.\n\nWe must use Node.js built-in http and sqlite. No external deps.\n\nWe need to set up npm start script that runs server.js.\n\nImplement SQLite DB with table projects (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL). Use DB_PATH env var.\n\nServer must serve static files from public folder, handle API endpoints:\n\n- GET /health -\u003e JSON\n\n- GET /api/projects -\u003e list projects\n\n- POST /api/projects -\u003e create project; body JSON {name}. Trim, if empty return 400 with error message.\n\n- GET /api/projects/:id -\u003e get single project.\n\nPotentially also serve project page.\n\nBut front-end can just navigate to /projects/\u003cid\u003e which is served by static file (maybe same index.html with routing client-side). Simpler: server serves same index.html for any path (except API and /health). Use fallback.\n\nImplement client: At '/' show heading, input, button, list.\n\nWhen button clicked, send POST to /api/projects, then refresh list.\n\nWhen list shows rows with data-testid=\"project-row\" and button Open project linking to /projects/\u003cid\u003e.\n\nOn /projects/\u003cid\u003e page, display heading with project name and button back.\n\nWe can implement a simple SPA using vanilla JS with hash or path detection. Since we serve same HTML, client script reads location.pathname, decides view.\n\nImplement alert for validation error: show visible alert element.\n\nNeed to ensure data persists via SQLite file.\n\nImplement npm start script in package.json: \"start\": \"node server.js\".\n\nNo external deps; we must use node:sqlite (experimental). Actually Node 22 includes built-in sqlite module? Node has \"node:sqlite\" experimental API. We'll use that.\n\nWrite server.js using import syntax (ES modules). Use http, fs, path, url, sqlite.\n\nImplement async initialization of DB.\n\nServe static files: read files from public folder.\n\nFor any request not starting with /api or /health, serve index.html.\n\nImplement API endpoints.\n\nNow we need to commit changes. Use git commands.\n\nFirst, list repo files.","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

