le.\n\nImplement npm start script in package.json: \"start\": \"node server.js\".\n\nNo external deps; we must use node:sqlite (experimental). Actually Node 22 includes built-in sqlite module? Node has \"node:sqlite\" experimental API. We'll use that.\n\nWrite server.js using import syntax (ES modules). Use http, fs, path, url, sqlite.\n\nImplement async initialization of DB.\n\nServe static files: read files from public folder.\n\nFor any request not starting with /api or /health, serve index.html.\n\nImplement API endpoints.\n\nNow we need to commit changes. Use git commands.\n\nFirst, list repo files.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":467,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

